course: dictionary
lesson: 4844
title: Hydrogen, the lightest element
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An element is a substance made of only one kind of atom. Hydrogen is the lightest of all the elements. It is a gas with no colour, smell or taste, and its chemical symbol is H.
explain: Hydrogen is the most common element in the universe, and it is number 1 in the periodic table, the chart that lists all the elements. Stars like the Sun are mostly made of hydrogen and helium.
explain: Atoms join together to make new things. «H2O» means two hydrogen atoms joined to one oxygen atom: that is one molecule of water. The little 2 tells you there are two hydrogen atoms.
fact: Hydrogen is the lightest chemical element and the most common element in the universe.
fact: Hydrogen is a gas with no colour, smell or taste, and it burns easily.
fact: The chemical symbol for hydrogen is H.
fact: Deep in the Sun, at about 15 million °C, hydrogen is squeezed into helium, and this gives out enormous energy.
fact: The Sun shines because tiny parts of hydrogen join together, a process called fusion, and it will keep shining for about another five billion years.
exercise: What is the chemical symbol for hydrogen? | Hd | *H | Hy | Ho
exercise: «H2O» means two hydrogen atoms joined to one oxygen atom. What is that called? | One atom of oxygen | A salt crystal | *One molecule of water | Two stars
exercise: Which statement about hydrogen is true? | It is the heaviest of all the elements | It is a blue solid like ice | *It is the lightest of all the elements | It has a strong smell like rotten eggs
test: Which word means a substance made of only one kind of atom? | *Element | Fuel | Molecule | Fusion
test: Where does the Sun get its energy from? | Cold ice melting slowly | Oxygen burning in the air | *Hydrogen turning into helium deep inside | Dust from passing comets
exam: Why is hydrogen used as a fuel for some buses and rockets? | It is heavy and slows them down | *It burns easily and is a clean fuel | It is only found in the sea | It is solid and heavy like rock
